Evaluating $\dfrac{dy}{dx}$ at $\blueD{\theta = \dfrac{\pi}{2}}$ gives us the slope of our tangent line.

$\begin{align}
\greenD{\left. \dfrac{dy}{dx}\right| _{\theta=\tfrac{\pi}{6}}}&=\dfrac{\sin\left(\blueD{\dfrac{\pi}{2}}\right)+\left(\blueD{\dfrac{\pi}{2}}\right)\cos\left(\blueD{\dfrac{\pi}{2}}\right)}{\cos\left(\blueD{\dfrac{\pi}{2}}\right)-\left(\blueD{\dfrac{\pi}{2}}\right)\sin\left(\blueD{\dfrac{\pi}{2}}\right)} 
\\\\
&=\dfrac{1+\left(\dfrac{\pi}{2}\right)(0)}{0-\dfrac{\pi}{2}(1)}
\\\\
&=\greenD{-\dfrac{2}{\pi}}
\end{align}$
